<Layouts.marketing current_path={assigns[:current_path]} flash={@flash} current_scope={@current_scope} page_title={@page_title}>
  <%!-- ───────────── HERO ───────────── --%>
  <section class="bg-base-200 border-b border-base-300">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 py-14 lg:py-20 text-center">
      <.eyebrow name="pricing" align="center" />
      <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold tracking-tight leading-[1.05] mt-3">
        Free to build. <span class="text-primary">$100 a month</span> to run.
      </h1>
      <p class="text-lg text-base-content/70 mt-5 max-w-2xl mx-auto leading-relaxed">
        CodeMySpec is a set of AI harnesses that help one person build, sell, and support
        real software. Building is free forever. You pay when your software is live and working
        for you — or bring John in to build it with you.
      </p>
      <p class="text-sm text-base-content/60 mt-4">
        We never mark up the AI that powers it — bring your own keys and pay the AI company directly.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <%!-- ───────────── PLANS ───────────── --%>
  <section class="border-b border-base-300">
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6 py-16 lg:py-24">
      <.pricing_tiers />
    </div>
  </section>

  <%!-- ───────────── HOW THE MODEL WORKS ───────────── --%>
  <section class="border-b border-base-300 bg-base-200">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 py-14 lg:py-20">
      <.eyebrow name="how_it_works" />
      <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight mt-3">
        We make money when your software runs, not when you build it.
      </h2>
      <p class="text-lg text-base-content/70 mt-4 leading-relaxed">
        That's the whole model. Building costs us nothing to give away because you bring your
        own AI keys and pay the AI company directly — so the harness and the content engine are
        free forever, and your code is yours from the first commit. The $100 a month starts when
        your software is live and working for you: customer email on your own domain, live chat
        with a shared inbox, content publishing, Google Ads, and reporting that shows you who's
        converting. And if you'd rather not drive the build yourself, John runs the harness on
        your project with you — same specs, same tests, same verification — scoped and quoted
        after a real conversation.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <%!-- ───────────── FAQ ───────────── --%>
  <section class="border-b border-base-300">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 py-14 lg:py-20">
      <.eyebrow name="fair_questions" />
      <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight mt-3">
        Pricing questions, answered straight.
      </h2>
      <div class="mt-8 space-y-8">
        <div>
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold">How much does CodeMySpec cost?</h3>
          <p class="text-base-content/70 mt-2 leading-relaxed">
            Building is free forever. Running your software — customer email on your domain,
            live chat, content publishing, ads, and conversion reporting — is $100 a month per
            user. If you want it built with you, John quotes the work after a conversation,
            with a $500 minimum.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold">Is the free tier a trial?</h3>
          <p class="text-base-content/70 mt-2 leading-relaxed">
            No. The build harness and the content engine are free forever, with no credit card
            and nothing that expires. It isn't a stripped-down demo — it's the same harness
            John uses to run CodeMySpec itself.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold">Am I paying for the AI on top of this?</h3>
          <p class="text-base-content/70 mt-2 leading-relaxed">
            You bring your own AI keys and pay the AI company directly for what you use.
            CodeMySpec never marks up model tokens or proxies your requests — your keys, your
            bill, your code.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold">What does "per user" mean?</h3>
          <p class="text-base-content/70 mt-2 leading-relaxed">
            A user is a person on your account doing the work — answering chat, sending email,
            publishing content. If that's just you, Operate &amp; Grow costs $100 a month,
            total. Add seats only when more hands are actually in the tools.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold">What does the $500 minimum on Built with you cover?</h3>
          <p class="text-base-content/70 mt-2 leading-relaxed">
            It's a floor, not a package. You bring what you're trying to run, John scopes it in
            a real conversation and quotes a real number. The work is done the same way as
            self-serve — specs, tests, verification — and you own everything when it ships.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold">What happens if I stop paying?</h3>
          <p class="text-base-content/70 mt-2 leading-relaxed">
            The hosted services stop — email, chat, publishing, reporting. Your software, your
            code, and your content stay yours. There's no lock-in to unwind; the $100 was never
            rent on your own app.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold">Can I use it for internal tools instead of software I sell?</h3>
          <p class="text-base-content/70 mt-2 leading-relaxed">
            Yes. Build and Operate work the same whether the software faces customers or your
            own crew. Plenty of operators need a tool that fits their workflow, not a product
            to sell — that counts.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <%!-- ───────────── RECOMMENDED PATH ───────────── --%>
  <section class="border-b border-base-300 bg-base-200">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 py-14 lg:py-20">
      <.eyebrow name="where_to_start" />
      <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight mt-3">
        Start with the marketing, not the app.
      </h2>
      <p class="text-lg text-base-content/70 mt-4 leading-relaxed">
        The harness includes a content engine, so the free tier isn't a demo — it's a working
        start. Spin up your site, publish content, and let people find you while the software
        is still being built. By the time the app is ready, you have an audience waiting for it.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap gap-4">
        <.link href={~p"/install"} class="btn btn-primary btn-lg" data-event-label="cta-start-free-pricing-page">Start free</.link>
        <a href={ExternalLinks.cal_john()} class="btn btn-outline btn-lg" data-event-label="cta-service-inquiry-pricing-page">Talk to John</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <%!-- The buying half. Nested rather than replacing this page: it is a dead
       view with canonical/og tags and no socket, and only buyers need one.
       Must sit INSIDE Layouts.marketing — outside it, this rendered below the
       footer, where nobody would ever scroll to buy. --%>
  <section class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 pb-16">
    {live_render(@conn, CodeMySpecWeb.CheckoutLive, id: "checkout-live")}
  </section>

</Layouts.marketing>
